1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,203
Zoya has one big question.

2
00:00:02,203 --> 00:00:04,107
How do we sell more laddoos?

3
00:00:04,407 --> 00:00:06,005
Arjun says, make more.

4
00:00:06,005 --> 00:00:07,850
Nani says, make it better.

5
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:09,448
Dev says, push harder.

6
00:00:09,798 --> 00:00:13,157
Each answer is a way of
thinking, called an orientation.

7
00:00:13,757 --> 00:00:17,268
An orientation is where a
business points its attention.

8
00:00:17,568 --> 00:00:18,784
At the factory.

9
00:00:18,784 --> 00:00:19,784
The product.

10
00:00:19,784 --> 00:00:20,684
Selling.

11
00:00:20,515 --> 00:00:21,566
The customer.

12
00:00:21,566 --> 00:00:22,514
Or society.

13
00:00:23,114 --> 00:00:25,003
So what are marketing concepts?

14
00:00:25,303 --> 00:00:27,118
Philip Kotler lists five.

15
00:00:27,118 --> 00:00:30,288
Each one is a belief
about why customers buy.

16
00:00:30,638 --> 00:00:31,538
Production.

17
00:00:31,533 --> 00:00:32,433
Product.

18
00:00:32,272 --> 00:00:33,172
Selling.

19
00:00:33,012 --> 00:00:33,912
Marketing.

20
00:00:33,855 --> 00:00:35,500
And societal marketing.

21
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:37,000
One.

22
00:00:36,611 --> 00:00:38,195
The production concept.

23
00:00:38,195 --> 00:00:41,143
People want what is
cheap and easy to find.

24
00:00:41,443 --> 00:00:45,178
So Arjun makes two hundred
laddoos a day, at a lower cost.

25
00:00:45,478 --> 00:00:47,874
But nobody asked who wants two hundred.

26
00:00:48,424 --> 00:00:49,324
Two.

27
00:00:48,944 --> 00:00:50,404
The product concept.

28
00:00:50,404 --> 00:00:52,445
People want the best quality.

29
00:00:52,745 --> 00:00:56,192
Nani adds almonds and
saffron, and the price climbs.

30
00:00:56,492 --> 00:00:59,280
But parents only wanted
a simple tiffin snack.

31
00:00:59,830 --> 00:01:00,730
Three.

32
00:01:00,428 --> 00:01:01,830
The selling concept.

33
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:03,849
People must be pushed to buy.

34
00:01:04,149 --> 00:01:08,054
Dev prints posters, and Arjun
shouts deals at the college gate.

35
00:01:08,354 --> 00:01:10,636
Sales jump for a week, then fall.

36
00:01:10,636 --> 00:01:12,616
Pushed buyers rarely come back.

37
00:01:13,166 --> 00:01:14,066
Four.

38
00:01:13,705 --> 00:01:15,175
The marketing concept.

39
00:01:15,175 --> 00:01:18,876
Find what customers need, and
serve it better than others.

40
00:01:19,176 --> 00:01:22,981
Busy parents want small laddoos,
in a six pack for tiffins.

41
00:01:23,281 --> 00:01:24,181
Mrs.

42
00:01:23,806 --> 00:01:26,926
Rao buys every week,
and sales keep growing.

43
00:01:27,476 --> 00:01:28,376
Five.

44
00:01:28,042 --> 00:01:30,106
The societal marketing concept.

45
00:01:30,106 --> 00:01:33,526
Serve customers, and protect
people and the planet.

46
00:01:33,826 --> 00:01:35,823
Nani keeps refined sugar out.

47
00:01:35,823 --> 00:01:38,281
Dev picks paper packs, not plastic.

48
00:01:38,581 --> 00:01:41,188
Good for the child, the
family, and the city.

49
00:01:41,788 --> 00:01:44,123
The first three start from what you make.

50
00:01:44,123 --> 00:01:45,937
The last two start from people.

51
00:01:46,637 --> 00:01:51,915
In 1960, Theodore Levitt wrote Marketing
Myopia, in the Harvard Business

52
00:01:51,915 --> 00:01:52,815
Review.

53
00:01:52,987 --> 00:01:54,673
Myopia means short sight.

54
00:01:54,973 --> 00:01:57,579
His example was the American railroads.

55
00:01:57,579 --> 00:01:59,666
People still needed to travel.

56
00:01:59,966 --> 00:02:03,084
But cars, trucks and planes
took those customers.

57
00:02:03,384 --> 00:02:08,118
Levitt said the railroads were product
oriented, instead of customer oriented.

58
00:02:08,718 --> 00:02:11,715
So Zoya asks, what
business are we really in?

59
00:02:12,015 --> 00:02:13,011
Not laddoos.

60
00:02:13,011 --> 00:02:14,584
Healthy tiffin snacks.

61
00:02:14,584 --> 00:02:17,697
So biscuits, fruit and
chips are rivals too.

62
00:02:18,297 --> 00:02:20,077
Where do we see these five today?

63
00:02:20,377 --> 00:02:21,287
Production.

64
00:02:21,287 --> 00:02:24,718
A budget airline cuts
costs, so fares stay low.

65
00:02:25,018 --> 00:02:25,918
Product.

66
00:02:25,748 --> 00:02:28,980
A phone maker adds a
sharper camera every year.

67
00:02:29,280 --> 00:02:30,180
Selling.

68
00:02:29,968 --> 00:02:32,858
An insurance agent calls
you again and again.

69
00:02:33,158 --> 00:02:34,058
Marketing.

70
00:02:33,976 --> 00:02:37,411
A bank adds the app features
its customers ask for.

71
00:02:37,711 --> 00:02:38,611
Societal.

72
00:02:38,562 --> 00:02:42,602
A food delivery app lets you
say no to plastic spoons.

73
00:02:43,202 --> 00:02:45,533
But is caring for society easy?

74
00:02:45,533 --> 00:02:46,526
Not always.

75
00:02:46,826 --> 00:02:47,869
The good side.

76
00:02:47,869 --> 00:02:50,847
Customers trust you, and
the city stays cleaner.

77
00:02:51,147 --> 00:02:52,249
The hard side.

78
00:02:52,249 --> 00:02:54,402
It costs more, and takes time.

79
00:02:54,702 --> 00:02:57,094
Dev's paper pack costs four rupees.

80
00:02:57,094 --> 00:02:58,957
The plastic one cost two.

81
00:02:59,257 --> 00:03:03,394
Zoya keeps the price at a hundred
and twenty, and earns less per pack.

82
00:03:03,694 --> 00:03:09,786
Since July 2022, India has banned many
single use plastics, even the film

83
00:03:09,786 --> 00:03:11,322
on sweet boxes.

84
00:03:11,622 --> 00:03:12,522
The lesson?

85
00:03:12,485 --> 00:03:14,940
Serve your customers, and do no harm.

86
00:03:15,540 --> 00:03:16,507
Quick check.

87
00:03:16,507 --> 00:03:20,863
Laddoo Lab serves busy parents, and
switches to paper packs to protect

88
00:03:20,863 --> 00:03:21,763
the city.

89
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:23,265
Which concept is this?

90
00:03:25,165 --> 00:03:26,475
Societal marketing!

91
00:03:26,475 --> 00:03:29,939
It serves the customer, and
looks after society too.

92
00:03:30,539 --> 00:03:31,548
So, remember.

93
00:03:31,848 --> 00:03:36,408
There are five concepts: production,
product, selling, marketing and societal

94
00:03:36,408 --> 00:03:37,308
marketing.

95
00:03:37,512 --> 00:03:39,811
The first three start from the business.

96
00:03:39,811 --> 00:03:42,102
Marketing starts from the customer's need.

97
00:03:42,452 --> 00:03:46,234
And societal marketing also
protects people and the planet.

98
00:03:46,834 --> 00:03:50,112
Next time, we'll explore
needs, wants and demands.
